      "content": "The issue you're experiencing could be due to improper sublimation ink viscosity or compatibility with the polyester blend you're using, possibly caused by a variation in the polymer composition. It is crucial that the ink is formulated to bond at the temperatures and pressures you're using. Assess whether the frost has been uniformly applied and that the inks haven't exhausted or are not evenly distributing on the polyester. Ensuring the ink level on the sublimation paper is consistent and removing any residual water from the polyester before sublimation are also factors to consider. It's advisable to conduct a material test print with a section of the polyester to verify the ink's adherence and color saturation before applying it to the entire batch.",
